diff --git a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
index 6bddff1..aba2bf5 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
@@ -96,3 +96,41 @@ __Request:__
 __Response:__
 
 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
+## `POST /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions`
+
+Registers the current browser's Web Push subscription for the authenticated user. Users may only manage their own subscriptions, including when they are account administrators. Posting the same endpoint again updates its keys without creating another device subscription.
+
+__Request:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "push_subscription": {
+    "endpoint": "https://push-service.example/subscription-endpoint",
+    "p256dh_key": "browser-subscription-public-key",
+    "auth_key": "browser-subscription-auth-secret"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+All three fields are required. `p256dh_key` and `auth_key` are the browser subscription's `keys.p256dh` and `keys.auth`, not the application's VAPID keys. The endpoint must use HTTPS.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the subscription's `id` and a `Location` header identifying the subscription. Invalid subscriptions return `422 Unprocessable Entity`.
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5va03bpuvkcjemcxl73ho2"
+}
+```
+
+Subscribed devices receive the same title and body as the notification tray. Clicking a push opens the account-scoped card, including the comment anchor when applicable.
+
+## `DELETE /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions/:id`
+
+Unregisters one of the authenticated user's devices for this account. Other devices and account memberships are not affected.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `204 No Content` on success, or `404 Not Found` if the subscription does not belong to the user.
