@@ -101,6 +101,22 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+To let people receive their tray notifications on their phones and desktops, set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to a Web Push VAPID key pair. Use the same pair in the web and background-job containers, and keep it stable across deployments. The private key must remain secret; only the public key is sent to browsers.
+
+You can generate a pair once with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Optionally set `VAPID_SUBJECT` to a contact URL or `mailto:` address for your deployment. It defaults to `https://fizzy.do`.
+
+Push requires HTTPS (or localhost for development) and a running background-job worker. Users enable it separately on each device from **Notification Settings → Push Notifications**. On iOS, they must first add Fizzy to their Home Screen. The settings page includes browser-specific help for blocked notifications.
+
+Without both VAPID keys, push is unavailable; tray and email notifications continue to work normally.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
